# Environment for rabbithole. Copy to .env (gitignored, keep it private) and fill in.
#
# The binary reads ./.env itself on every command. Only RABBITHOLE_* keys are
# used, and a variable already set in the real environment wins over this file.
# Use --env-file to read another path. `make setup` creates .env from this file.
#
# Format: KEY=value, one per line. An optional leading `export ` is accepted, and
# one matching pair of single or double quotes around the value is removed.
# Nothing is expanded, and a `#` inside a value is kept. Lines starting with `#`
# are comments. For systemd, EnvironmentFile= reads plain KEY=value lines, or export
# the variables in your shell profile instead.
#
# `make` does not read this file; the binary does. A RABBITHOLE_DB set in your
# shell is respected by make, and DB= on the make command line wins when set.

# Bearer token for a hosted inference endpoint (OpenAI, a gateway, a protected
# vLLM). The settings store only the reference $RABBITHOLE_INFERENCE_API_KEY,
# never the value. Set `api_key: $RABBITHOLE_INFERENCE_API_KEY` in your config,
# or import a file with a literal api_key and rabbithole moves it here for you.
# RABBITHOLE_INFERENCE_API_KEY=

# The summary backend's token, when inference.summary uses its own endpoint.
# RABBITHOLE_SUMMARY_API_KEY=

# Where the store lives. Optional: unset uses the per-user data directory.
# A path is SQLite; a postgres:// URL is Postgres. Run `rabbithole store path`
# to see what is in use.
# RABBITHOLE_DB=

# Postgres only. The password for the RABBITHOLE_DB url, so it stays out of the
# URL. Ignored by SQLite.
# RABBITHOLE_DB_PASSWORD=
